`parse_configuration` and `parse_interface` in the same file already do this correctly (they decrement `size` and check `bLength > size`). Looks like `parse_iad_array` was written without the same convention.

### Reproducer (9 bytes)

```
08 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 ff
```

### ASAN output (driving `parse_iad_array` from the same verify harness)

```
==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow
READ of size 1 at 0x... (0 bytes after 9-byte region)
    #0 parse_iad_array descriptor.c:1381
```

Reachable via `libusb_get_active_interface_association_descriptors` / `libusb_get_interface_association_descriptors`. 1 byte OOB read, so usually silent on stock allocators but a DoS under hardened ones (GuardMalloc, ASAN deployments, etc.).

### Suggested fix

```diff
-        else if (header.bLength > size) {
+        else if (header.bLength > size - consumed) {
             usbi_warn(ctx, "short config descriptor read %d/%u",
-                      size, header.bLength);
+                      size - consumed, header.bLength);
             return LIBUSB_ERROR_IO;
         }
```

---

Both fixes are 1 line each. I have a PR ready that includes both fixes plus a new `tests/fuzz/fuzz_ss_ep_companion.c` harness for OSS-Fuzz coverage (the same harness that surfaces both bugs). Happy to open it whenever you've had a chance to confirm.

----
The attachments:

[fuzz_ss_ep_companion.c](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27081613/fuzz_ss_ep_companion.c)
[verify.c](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27081614/verify.c)

1. **`verify.c`** ：the unity-include verifier referenced in the body. Reproduces both bugs against libusb's actual `descriptor.c` source.
2. **`fuzz_ss_ep_companion.c`**： the single libFuzzer harness that surfaces both bugs (Bug A in ~1 second; Bug B from a 9-byte minimized input on the same corpus).

